{"decl":"TriangleFree","line":8,"plain":"A k-colouring C of the edges of K_n has no monochromatic triangle: each colour class graph is K_3-free.","standard_concept":"triangle-free (no monochromatic triangle) edge colouring","matches_standard":"yes","note":""},
{"decl":"ForcesMonochromaticTriangle","line":12,"plain":"Every k-colouring of the edges of K_n contains a monochromatic triangle.","standard_concept":"n ≥ R_k(3) in the Ramsey sense","matches_standard":"yes","note":"For k = 0 and n ≥ 2 there are no labelings, so the statement holds vacuously. This is irrelevant for the asymptotics."},
{"decl":"triangleRamseyNumber","line":15,"plain":"R_k(3) = least n such that every k-colouring of K_n has a monochromatic triangle.","standard_concept":"multicolour Ramsey number R(3,...,3) with k colours","matches_standard":"yes","note":"sInf over ℕ would be 0 if the set were empty. For k ≥ 1 the set is nonempty by Ramsey's theorem, so there is no junk issue."}
],
"lean_claims": [
{"theorem":"erdos_183","line":18,"plain":"R_k(3)^{1/k} → +∞ as k → ∞ (real rpow, filter atTop on both sides)."},
{"theorem":"erdos_problem_183_explicit","line":25,"plain":"For every k ≥ 2, (k^{1/3} / (6 e^{38} log k))^k ≤ R_k(3), and R_k(3)^{1/k} → ∞."},
{"theorem":"triangleRamseyNumber_log_sharp_coefficients","line":36,"plain":"There exists a real ε such that, if 0 < ε, then eventually in k: (1/3 - ε) k log k ≤ log R_k(3) ≤ (1+ε) k log k. Taking ε ≤ 0 makes it trivially true."},
{"theorem":"triangleRamseyNumber_log_isTheta","line":45,"plain":"log R_k(3) = Θ(k log k) as k → ∞."}
],
"paper_claims": [
{"ref":"Theorem 1.1","plain":"There is an absolute constant c > 0 such that R_k(3) ≥ (c k^{1/3} / log k)^k for all k ≥ 2."},
{"ref":"Theorem 1.1 (consequences)","plain":"k^{(1/3 - o(1))k} ≤ R_k(3) ≤ k^{(1+o(1))k}, so R_k(3) = k^{Θ(k)}."},
{"ref":"Eq. (4)","plain":"lim R_k(3)^{1/k} = +∞."}
